title: "Generalization of AI-Generated Image Detectors Across GAN and Diffusion Models: Detection and Attribution of Known and Unseen Generators"
abstract: "AI-Fake-Image-Detector is an open-source deep learning framework designed to evaluate the generalization capability of image forgery detectors across Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) and modern Diffusion models (Stable Diffusion 2.1/3/XL, DALL-E 3, Midjourney v6). The system performs both binary Real vs. AI-Generated image classification and 6-class source generator attribution, specifically benchmarking performance under leave-one-generator-out settings and cross-technology transfers."
date-released: 2026-10-10
url: "https://github.com/m-eshan/AI-Fake-Image-Detector"
repository-code: "https://github.com/m-eshan/AI-Fake-Image-Detector"
keywords:
  - AI Image Detection
  - Deepfake Forensics
  - Generative Adversarial Networks
  - Diffusion Models
  - Transfer Learning
  - Generator Attribution
  - Synthetic Media Forensics
